#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157072 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "21071a31-a79e-5aa4-9a57-8ce642770adb" :question/math-academy-id "e-7663" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {11}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}}{{11}^{x}} & \\ge {11}^{x}\\cdot 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-8)^{3} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-8)^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-8 & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{8} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -2\\sqrt 2$ or $x \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "9e1ccbcf-23bb-5df5-aa02-cb90a9421396" :question/math-academy-id "e-7664" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1} .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <-x{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{x+1}+x{e}^{x+1}-2{e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-2){e}^{x+1} & <0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1){e}^{x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) <   0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 <   x <   1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/2f01104ae0cb9a41c5c5e4b8393e346f7d0e9b2bfd1afa593ee6bdfb0fff39f2.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 <   x <   1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "35c42ff1-2381-5fb4-b04b-cbe790e1d667" :question/math-academy-id "e-7665" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >{4}^{x-15} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{x}-{4}^{x-15} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{-15})\\cdot {4}^{x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5} & >{4}^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & >\\sqrt[5]{{4}^{-15}} \\\\ x & >{({4}^{-15})}^{1/5} \\\\ x & >{4}^{-3} \\\\ x & >\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x > \\dfrac{1}{64}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dadc738-d4d0-597e-ac4c-f9a561e8fceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300622} {:answer/id #uuid "846d1070-81b9-593e-af5c-2c18ab33cc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300623} {:answer/id #uuid "04197ece-15d0-5cff-916b-3a3bb8d4093f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300624} {:answer/id #uuid "34d1d205-798a-52d6-a246-86c00e9d0375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300625} {:answer/id #uuid "b5809cd6-a6be-5e5d-a775-7e24437d8391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "846d1070-81b9-593e-af5c-2c18ab33cc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300623} :answer-field/id #uuid "1350abaa-be9e-5288-b428-4417f3430e7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f6ef83f-0afe-5013-adb1-85c6601a8666" :question/math-academy-id "q-115404" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by $(0.33)^{2x-5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(4{x}^{6}+3)\\cdot (0.33)^{2x-5}}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{(0.33)^{2x-5}} \\\\ 4{x}^{6}+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFurthermore, $4{x}^{6}+3\\ge 0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the solution is all real numbers."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "209aff17-19fb-5ad1-bcec-278429f58b3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300629} {:answer/id #uuid "e6309cad-e51b-5ab6-b46b-f41107376365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300630} {:answer/id #uuid "81303778-c0bf-59b9-8ff9-75a5717f87a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300631} {:answer/id #uuid "2136567f-782c-5036-8093-c4022d3e5876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300632} {:answer/id #uuid "3da5bd22-6bdc-5fb9-8557-76136b98c398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da5bd22-6bdc-5fb9-8557-76136b98c398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300633} :answer-field/id #uuid "69595d5a-01f8-53b7-8e8d-77b5b4386bcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94195579-c6ea-570a-b6e8-8733c4f53017" :question/math-academy-id "q-115408" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}<0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${3}^{x+6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{(2x-5)^{3}\\cdot {3}^{x+6}}{{3}^{x+6}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+6}} \\\\ (2x-5)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(2x-5)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ 2x-5 & <0 \\\\ 2x & <5 \\\\ x & <\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8f03f67-cbf3-5232-bf22-ba3d279ea411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300636} {:answer/id #uuid "46580a3e-f091-5d54-a45d-e2e6573aec63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300637} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc66538-8e90-5708-a442-79c29c5089a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300638} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff8bf2b-011b-5172-ae59-104a9f628c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300639} {:answer/id #uuid "271a0841-346a-56be-8d84-3edc4cc0f80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ff8bf2b-011b-5172-ae59-104a9f628c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300639} :answer-field/id #uuid "1011c311-018e-53cb-846e-56fb5080e8eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29e3d62b-d100-50a8-8289-45e98db458c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-115410" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}}<0.$" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $(0.6)^{3x-2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}} & <0 \\\\ (0.6)^{3x-2}\\cdot \\frac{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}}{(0.6)^{3x-2}} & <(0.6)^{3x-2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-4)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-4 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <4 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{4} \\\\ |x| & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd0d5925-ae67-5cd7-a980-635fed6b60e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300643} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e3bc25-6b40-57f4-aeb7-042bb248b5b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300644} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f80f8-ffe7-59f5-9e15-5dc18ac86477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300645} {:answer/id #uuid "4d04f1d3-5f95-5586-9004-29a38c36ce0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300646} {:answer/id #uuid "2941a21b-101a-53d0-85d8-cdb1a206a193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8e3bc25-6b40-57f4-aeb7-042bb248b5b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300644} :answer-field/id #uuid "65963c00-0a90-56b3-be61-6ec87889c2d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3754b800-5aa3-5f3a-a9b9-6e9a52514d6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-115429" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}\\ge -2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} & \\ge -2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} \\\\ 5x\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+4\\cdot {7}^{2x+3}+2\\cdot {7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+4+2){7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+6){7}^{2x+3} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{2x+3}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+6 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge -6 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x\\ge -\\frac{6}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c979272-a42e-5228-9785-f5ad5eec9c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300650} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb12ec1-c3b5-5401-892c-5b3277798689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300651} {:answer/id #uuid "595ca0b2-a773-57c9-bd9a-3633c10c523c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300652} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3556b8-8616-512b-b97b-0a07701d46fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2<x<5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300653} {:answer/id #uuid "3034693c-7fb3-5258-8954-9ad41a8e2b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfb12ec1-c3b5-5401-892c-5b3277798689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300651} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5bfae9-dccd-5239-9298-8bd3b14e5371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f16ad2b1-8aa8-5b8e-8f71-14422bf71237" :question/math-academy-id "q-115430" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}>-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} \\\\ 4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}+{6}^{3x-2}+{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ (4+1+{x}^{2}){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${6}^{3x-2}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+5 & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}^{2}+5>0$ for all values of $x,$ the solution is all real numbers."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f37478dc-c2a4-59f3-a681-6b20c6f03f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300657} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc406a4-745a-5081-97eb-37e89cb957db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300658} {:answer/id #uuid "26210814-24e8-5605-9cf0-343709fd0678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\le x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300659} {:answer/id #uuid "f445bcb0-fdc2-5103-b1e9-d485ce6f2d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300660} {:answer/id #uuid "5956da79-4dd5-5a86-b4bf-9699724313a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bc406a4-745a-5081-97eb-37e89cb957db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300658} :answer-field/id #uuid "b192b996-3d51-521d-b86e-6d2523d95a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c9c6c77-82d3-5846-97fb-06c132d49ce6" :question/math-academy-id "q-115450" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7}\\ge {2}^{2x-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7} & \\ge {2}^{2x-3} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{2x-7}-{2}^{2x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-{2}^{4})\\cdot {2}^{2x-7} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${2}^{2x-7}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{2}^{4}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{2}^{4} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{16} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e7aa91-1160-5a0e-a040-f84c54167cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300664} {:answer/id #uuid "838610dc-10fe-5461-a4a0-ab14bfe9a9e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<0$ or $x>7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300665} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbf0c20-a591-57ab-a8f4-bc262b5ad8f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-7$ or $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300666} {:answer/id #uuid "50709a7f-c906-53bf-a4d7-11cc095621b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300667} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cca57c-3a3f-5653-8ee2-40918e13312b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50709a7f-c906-53bf-a4d7-11cc095621b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300667} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbc38055-3f37-5023-a6f3-89fb88a1c93e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de4ed423-b3b6-523b-8fc2-12103a68a785" :question/math-academy-id "q-115458" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2}<-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+7x\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ x(x+7)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{4x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x+7)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-7$ and $x=0.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-7<x<0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/b884ee15f864bcd02639085dc1465a82958ef0faeb9408e68b405c5906ea3a18.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-7<x<0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30633f2e-b8f0-5161-b1a3-be7ff3d79bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300671} {:answer/id #uuid "5e813fc3-c0b5-5ba0-aa0f-99f46ce5dd5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge -2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300672} {:answer/id #uuid "a4503c9f-5956-518c-98de-e915186e0edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\le x\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300673} {:answer/id #uuid "efcffe95-d275-5257-831f-71649ed2d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300674} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9e4a17-ec5f-5177-96ca-2fd5cfa56375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30633f2e-b8f0-5161-b1a3-be7ff3d79bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300671} :answer-field/id #uuid "cacdec37-49f6-5f9b-b3f5-3ac10782c6c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d11be10-3811-5741-8980-d440f63a3049" :question/math-academy-id "q-115460" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2}\\le 2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{7x+2}-2x\\cdot {3}^{7x+3} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x\\cdot 3)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0 \\\\ x(x-6)\\cdot {3}^{7x+2} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{7x+2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-6)\\le 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=6.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis or touch this axis when $0\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/d75b387ac3e54f253eab62d9492b39f2744298e776f663d542b26e3c47f7d6a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44cf8eba-22ad-568d-84ed-a2295fdf914d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44cf8eba-22ad-568d-84ed-a2295fdf914d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300678} :answer-field/id #uuid "96352652-42ae-56a8-9893-0570b8a9ec28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcb6c826-cacf-579f-b2b7-33c7a1cdd65c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcb6c826-cacf-579f-b2b7-33c7a1cdd65c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300680} :answer-field/id #uuid "19832d7c-d976-5a81-a2c3-3b8e83c588aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48cca59-78f0-5760-925b-fdb9ff798be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48cca59-78f0-5760-925b-fdb9ff798be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300682} :answer-field/id #uuid "e913e3cc-4569-517b-8c8c-7686e4fd7d81" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eee0e3d3-41d0-5b08-ad62-df351dc1f2a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-276747" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-{2}^{2x-3}{x}^{2}+3x\\cdot {2}^{2x-3}>-4\\cdot {2}^{2x-3}.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{2}^{2x-3}{x}^{2}+3x\\cdot {2}^{2x-3} & >-4\\cdot {2}^{2x-3} \\\\ (-{x}^{2}+3x+4){2}^{2x-3} & >0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-3x-4){2}^{2x-3} & >0 \\\\ -(x+1)(x-4){2}^{2x-3} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${2}^{2x-3}$ and get\n\n$$\n-(x+1)(x-4)>0.\n$$\n\nThis represents a downwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-1$ and $x=4.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $-1<x<4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/df6c1c0ac26d9074f8c726b2265780fefad631561d7a729d2dfc7998ef043859.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-1<x<4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be2c4390-5877-5cea-9688-e8e9af667086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300685} {:answer/id #uuid "19c93f1d-b187-54cc-abfd-f476ee8f7d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be2c4390-5877-5cea-9688-e8e9af667086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300685} :answer-field/id #uuid "6591f3ae-a7ff-541a-98a5-1e7aac725f23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e89c13b1-c237-5019-95d5-e8b412f22da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e89c13b1-c237-5019-95d5-e8b412f22da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff80e483-9b77-55ce-9da3-e8d61e85fa89" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64614e5a-5e27-5008-b241-bb1397ae8b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64614e5a-5e27-5008-b241-bb1397ae8b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300690} :answer-field/id #uuid "e57f2583-737d-559b-9560-9c15e2914f02" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23c4ca3b-a23e-5058-8264-816d892804ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-278181" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}<0.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$<x$ \n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${2}^{3x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}}{{2}^{3x}} & <\\frac{0}{{2}^{3x}} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-25)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-25 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <25 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x| & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd362e21-5cdd-541a-a773-a0032f6122ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd362e21-5cdd-541a-a773-a0032f6122ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300693} :answer-field/id #uuid "43ff7341-8644-51ac-afe1-ef0830dc3ff3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7258ae2-184d-53bb-9f3a-43d391713394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7258ae2-184d-53bb-9f3a-43d391713394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300695} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4eadecf-dab9-5909-aa1a-f51ff976603c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a65eca1-5a10-5115-8d48-b3735395891f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a65eca1-5a10-5115-8d48-b3735395891f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300697} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ebb9c8-6590-5761-870b-c483fe403c17" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2be0e649-7ba0-5a50-84d9-4b69508aa9f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-278219" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}\\le 0.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${6}^{3x-2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & \\le 0 \\\\ \\frac{(49-{x}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}}{{6}^{3x-2}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{6}^{3x-2}} \\\\ (49-{x}^{2})^{3} & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(49-{x}^{2})^{3}} & \\le \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ 49-{x}^{2} & \\le 0 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & \\le -49 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 49 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{49} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign again of the inequality since we divided by a negative number ($-1$).\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -7$ or $x\\ge 7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c9112c0-826c-5530-b408-4a44cca8af76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300700} {:answer/id #uuid "921f5927-9ea9-5c23-87bd-6773602d1371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c9112c0-826c-5530-b408-4a44cca8af76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300700} :answer-field/id #uuid "e474a135-4a8d-5917-97e1-361ddde125fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e4151c8-cf8b-5346-9bdb-65030117bbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e4151c8-cf8b-5346-9bdb-65030117bbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300703} :answer-field/id #uuid "967efb26-8a8c-53da-babc-d97990daafa1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6e4ba0f-cd7a-58d2-bdc5-b12f24161589" :question/math-academy-id "q-278230" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1}\\ge -6\\cdot {3}^{x+1}.$\n\n$x$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1} & \\ge -6\\cdot {3}^{x+1} \\\\ 5x\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {3}^{x+1}+{3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+6+1){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (5x+7){3}^{x+1} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{x+1}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+7){3}^{x+1}}{{3}^{x+1}} & <\\frac{0}{{3}^{x+1}} \\\\ 5x+7 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge 0-7 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\ge -\\frac{7}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae02397f-5aa4-5322-8744-7b16342006b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae02397f-5aa4-5322-8744-7b16342006b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300706} :answer-field/id #uuid "839918da-bf53-5f3b-a165-15e48d53de70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300705} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44057b38-b9f3-583d-9557-dfa6f0ddb25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44057b38-b9f3-583d-9557-dfa6f0ddb25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300708} :answer-field/id #uuid "adb7d7d6-cfd7-589d-8267-4fc720149477" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed980dda-d4cb-57c3-93d9-bce62f13ecaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed980dda-d4cb-57c3-93d9-bce62f13ecaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300710} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d39ae47-17dc-595e-91d5-d5742dfb7731" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "635c959c-0b6c-521a-a003-0a8f98853fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-278239" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}>-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}.$\n\n$x<${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >-{5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2-7x}{x}^{2}-10\\cdot {5}^{2-7x}+3x\\cdot {5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+3x-10){5}^{2-7x} & >0 \\\\ (x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{2-7x}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+5)(x-2){5}^{2-7x}}{{5}^{2-7x}} & >\\frac{0}{{5}^{2-7x}} \\\\ (x+5)(x-2) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-5$ and $x=2.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $x<-5$ or $x>2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/6b72efca34700ab06986460d4d190e0e83a4f0068c9effe20af622082a92b9a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x<-5$ or $x>2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d1bdea7-a76b-565e-94fc-e9dfd0ec9090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300713} {:answer/id #uuid "7943d3f3-eb0c-5569-bff0-b8c289537e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7943d3f3-eb0c-5569-bff0-b8c289537e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300714} :answer-field/id #uuid "2196882d-9dee-581e-9b76-fdff84b5f4ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d39343-fce0-5c73-ae07-10d4d3659f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d39343-fce0-5c73-ae07-10d4d3659f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300716} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c954466-879d-5087-bbe2-5f59e286583c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79b77f2e-0951-53fc-92e6-58cdcac40f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-278271" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}\\le {4}^{4x+4}.$\n\n$x$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le {4}^{4x+4} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{4x+4} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}-{4}^{5}\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{4x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{5}-{4}^{5})\\cdot {4}^{4x-1}}{{4}^{4x-1}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{4}^{4x-1}} \\\\ ({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{5}-{4}^{5}) & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{5} & \\le {4}^{5} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & \\le \\sqrt[5]{{4}^{5}} \\\\ x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is $x\\le 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b282b7-3d62-5fbd-a721-e0e94c2a7181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le 0$ or $x \\ge 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156359} {:answer/id #uuid "0b53fec1-b30d-5d9f-a33c-665834a70977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 \\le x \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156360} {:answer/id #uuid "443d4ceb-d027-5ca0-8b57-a260f5bce1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156361} {:answer/id #uuid "548ece35-3b60-5221-997a-80ec664e36ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156362} {:answer/id #uuid "75c3926e-c51b-5d8c-8bdc-a57f69f13af3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le - 3$ or $x \\ge 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b282b7-3d62-5fbd-a721-e0e94c2a7181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le 0$ or $x \\ge 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156359} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a20aa5-2832-5d35-8d27-37e2cdef5624" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "485dd702-22ef-5672-ba6d-aa433fac1c74" :question/math-academy-id "q-87772" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${3}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\ge {3}^{4x+1}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4x}{x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{4x+1}x \\\\ {3}^{4x}{x}^{2}-{3}^{4x+1}x & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}({x}^{2}-3x) & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}x(x-3) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{4x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-3)\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is at or above the $x$-axis when $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/3bfb82543e7c05d0ca0b8f6c6973025400ad1253acbc57214173dbd3e8c37fef.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is  $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$"}]}
